# BeagleBone — Camera Manager

Manages all camera devices on the network. Receives UDP heartbeats from
ESP32-CAM and ESP32 doorbell devices, maintains a liveness registry, learns
camera IPs from incoming packets, and dispatches UDP CAPTURE triggers to
cameras on PIR occupancy events.

## Source Files

| File | Description |
|:-----|:------------|
| `camera_manager.c` | Main process — UDP ingress, IP registry, trigger dispatcher |
| `build_info.c` | Build timestamp |

## Architecture
ESP32-CAM (heartbeat UDP 9094)

│

▼

camera_manager

├── learns source IP from recvfrom()

├── stamps liveness per slot

├── writes CamData frame to /tmp/cam_pipe → controller

│

└── UNIX socket /tmp/cam_trigger.sock

│

▼ (CamTriggerRequest from controller)

lookup cam IP + verify online

│

▼

UDP CAPTURE:event_id=...,zone=... → cam:9091

## Ports

| Port | Protocol | Direction | Purpose |
|------|----------|-----------|---------|
| 9094 | UDP | inbound | Heartbeats from all camera devices |
| 9091 | UDP | outbound | CAPTURE triggers to ESP32-CAM |
| 9092 | UDP | outbound | Doorbell press forwarding to hub |

## IPC

| Path | Type | Direction | Purpose |
|------|------|-----------|---------|
| `/tmp/cam_pipe` | Named FIFO | outbound | Camera liveness frames to controller |
| `/tmp/cam_trigger.sock` | UNIX datagram | inbound | PIR trigger requests from controller |

See `../include/cam_trigger_ipc.h` for the trigger IPC contract.
See `../include/ipc_proto.h` for the `CamData` pipe frame layout.

## Dependencies

```bash
sudo apt install gcc-arm-linux-gnueabihf
```

## Build

```bash
export ARCH=arm
export CROSS_COMPILE=arm-linux-gnueabihf-
cd ~/embedded-iot-hub/beaglebone/camera_manager

arm-linux-gnueabihf-gcc -g -O0 \
  camera_manager.c build_info.c \
  -o camera_manager \
  -I../include \
  -lpthread

# Verify architecture
file camera_manager
# Expected: ELF 32-bit LSB pie executable, ARM...
```

## Deploy

```bash
sudo systemctl stop camera-manager
scp camera_manager debian@beaglebone.local:~/camera_manager/camera_manager
sudo systemctl start camera-manager
tail -f /var/log/camera_manager.log
```

## Service Notes

`camera-manager.service` depends on `data-controller.service` and uses
`ExecStartPre` to wait until `/tmp/cam_pipe` exists before starting.
This prevents a deadlock where `camera_manager` attempts to open the
write end of the pipe before the controller has opened the read end.
